From b6037ac78e42dfd3fe6c618e8e12c14d5f925bcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:20:09 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: add xRX500 central DMA controller driver
 (hdma)

Add the driver for the xRX500 central DMA engines. Four controller
instances serve the ethernet datapath (DMA1TX, DMA1RX, DMA2TX,
DMA2RX); each is reset and configured at postcore probe (packet
arbitration, descriptor fetch-on-demand, flow control, byte enable,
global polling), then per-port and per-channel state is programmed:
port control 0x1F03, channel control/class, interrupt status clear
with interrupts left disabled - the CBM, not the CPU, services these
channels in steady state. Clocks are deliberately left untouched:
the boot chain hands over running clocks (see the clk driver's
CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED policy).

The channel-level API (ltq_request_dma, ltq_dma_chan_on/off/reset,
descriptor allocation and window configuration, IRQ enable/disable)
is consumed by the CBM patches that follow. Two details learned on
hardware are embedded here:

 - Channel-config faithfulness: the vendor never zeroes
   CDBA/CDLEN/CDPTNR when (re)configuring a live channel, and the
   DMA interrupt-enable mask must keep the egress channel bit set;
   deviating from either stalls the egress path. The V3
   memory-window readback used by other SoCs aliases onto DMA_CTRL
   on GRX500 and must not be read.

 - The controller pair can be cross-wired ("p2p"): a DMA1TX channel
   and a DMA2RX channel share one descriptor ring so switch-to-
   switch traffic moves without CPU involvement. dma_p2p_cfg() and
   the ring-seeding helper implement this; the CBM probe uses them
   to build the host-RX bridge. The 32-entry shared ring must be
   seeded with owned descriptors and data buffers before the pair
   is turned on - an unseeded ring is silently dead. Ring writes go
   through an uncached low-alias mapping of the ring memory so the
   seeds are visible to the engines on this non-coherent platform.

Ported from the AVM FRITZ!Box 7560 GPL release (Linux 4.9.198),
drivers/dma/intel/hdma.c/.h and include/linux/dma/lantiq_dmax.h -
Copyright (C) 2014-2015 Lei Chuanhua <chuanhua.lei@lantiq.com>,
